<title>USA: Virginia jobless rate rises to 4.5 pct in January.</title>
<headline>Virginia jobless rate rises to 4.5 pct in January.</headline>
<dateline>RICHMOND, Va. 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Virginia's unemployment rate rose to 4.5 percent in January from 4 percent in December, the state Employment Commission said Tueday.</p>
<p>Despite the monthly increase, the January rate was still the lowest for that month in eight years, and was down from 5.3 percent in January 1996, the commission said.</p>
<p>Lexington had the state's lowest unemployment rate, 1.6 percent, while Lancaster County had the highest, 25.3 percent.</p>
<p>--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013</p>
</text>
